# iPXE network boot (x86)

The default x86 build generates a standalone iPXE network-boot tree:

`boot-images/ipxe/efi-source/`

Serve this directory as both the TFTP root and HTTP document root.
The `boot/ipxe/autoexec.ipxe` script retrieves the kernel and initrd
over HTTP from DHCP's `next-server`.

| Firmware | DHCP boot filename |
| --- | --- |
| BIOS | `boot/ipxe/undionly.kpxe` |
| UEFI | `boot/ipxe/ipxe.efi` |
| UEFI Secure Boot | `boot/ipxe/snponly-shim.efi` |

Secure Boot requires the signed iPXE loader package. Fedora's signed
shim is staged under `EFI/BOOT/BOOTX64.EFI` for the UEFI kernel handoff.

After building, validate with `bash tests/verify-ipxe-output.sh`.
QEMU modes `bt net`, `bt net-efi`, and `bt net-efi-secure`
prefer the new tree, falling back to the legacy GRUB-staged tree.

**This produces network boot files, not a bootable ISO or USB/HDD image.**
For standalone local media, configure `param bootimages "grub"`
in the active `build.conf`. ARM continues to default to U-Boot.
